// Lesson template v4 (owner 2026-10-22: „много диктантов и исправления ошибок, разнообразия и ситуаций не хватает”;
// docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline with the course's people (docs/COURSE_CAST.md) and one goal,
// said on the first sheet: at the end the learner sends a warranty claim through a shop's e-service and writes a review
// of the service (054 Kasuta). Module 10's travel words come back all the time (rong, reis, lend, pilet, pagas,
// broneerima, tühistama, hilinema, sõitma).
//   051 Sofia's phone stayed on the train — the shop's offers, Sofia and the seller (listening), what a customer says;
//       Jaan buys suitcases for the family's flight to Rome; Oskar's football boots on a 60-euro budget.
//   052 Jaan looks for a used car — Jaan and Kadri compare two ads (listening); Viktor's three bikes for Oskar, Jaan
//       calls the seller (listening), Kadri's letter to Helgi; test drive and bargaining, a letter to the seller.
//   053 the phone does not charge — the shop's return and warranty terms; B1 grammar: participles as attributes
//       (ostetud kaup, makstud arve, avatud pakend, parandatud telefon, suletud konto; -tav / -v recognised: soovitatav,
//       müüdav, kehtiv); Sofia at the service desk (listening); Kadri's wrong parcel from an e-shop (call, letter).
//   054 Viktor sells bikes online — Jaan's instructions (listening), safe selling, the imperative; Viktor's call to
//       the bank (listening), Helgi's refund for a cancelled flight; the module project: the repaired phone breaks
//       again — a call to the manager, a warranty claim and a review. Participles come back in 054.
// Lesson 5 (055) is the module exam in Harno B1 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b1/module11.js, the v1
